title: National affairs
view-if: bruning_plot == "successful" and paramilitaries_timer == 0 and spd_in_government
frequency: 100
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/d_rose.jpg
on-arrival: {!
Q.military_supporting_right = (((Q.army_force * Q.military_available) * (1 - Q.reichswehr_loyalty)) / Q.army_force) * 100
Q.military_support_republic = ((Q.loyal_army * Q.military_available) / Q.army_force) * 100
!}
tags: fighting_paramilitaries

= National affairs

We cannot whether this storm alone, we need to cooperate lest we fall.

- @military_menu: The Military
- @dvp_menu: The DVP

@military_menu

Military supporting the right : [+ military_supporting_right +]%

Military supporting the republic : [+ military_support_republic +]%

Military loyalty : [+ reichswehr_loyalty : loyalty +]

- @promise_spending: We promise the army to fund them once this is over.
- @spending_1: We allocate a part of their budget to placate them.
- @delegate_1: We can delegate some of our paramilitary suppression operations to the Reichswehr.
- @spending_2: We can allocate a large portion of our budget on militarizing the Reichswehr even further.
- @delegate_2: We can give up major positions on anti streetfighting operations.
- @martial_law: With our situation, if it is better that Germany be under martial law than the extremists.
- @root: Perhaps another time
- @easy_discard


@promise_spending
view-if: military_concessions == 0
choose-if: military_weariness > 10
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.05; military_weariness -= 10; military_concessions = 1; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -=3; workers_nsdap += 3; unemployed_kpd += 3; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2
subtitle: A vague promise of future military funding. It buys us time, but at the cost of slight credibility.

@spending_1
view-if: military_concessions == 1
choose-if: military_weariness > 15
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.4; budget -= 1; military_weariness -= 25; military_concessions = 2; reichswehr_strength += 100; left_dissent += 10; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2
subtitle: A small part of the budget is reallocated to calm military leadership. -1 budget

The left our party are irritated. They cite it shows weakness, and could start a trend of once again, going to the military for help.

@delegate_1
view-if: military_concessions == 2
choose-if: military_weariness > 15
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.25; military_weariness -= 15; military_concessions = 3; rb_dissent += 25; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2
subtitle: We let the Reichswehr handle some suppression. This helps — but we lose some civilian oversight. The Reichsbanner are insulted by this. 

The Reichsbanner are untrusting of the Reichswehr, yet for now at least, most tolerate their presence.

@spending_2
view-if: military_concessions == 3
choose-if: military_weariness > 20
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.4; budget -=2; military_weariness -= 30; military_concessions = 4; reichswehr_militancy += 1; reichswehr_strength += 200; left_dissent += 25; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2
subtitle: A major boost to Reichswehr capabilities. Effective, but controversial. -2 budget

The left's fear have only grown worse, with many hardliners leaving the party and joining the KPD! Many in the party are starting to doubt our actions.

@delegate_2
view-if: military_concessions == 4
choose-if: military_weariness > 20
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.3; military_weariness -= 35; military_concessions = 5; rb_dissent = 100; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2
subtitle: We relinquish full operational control in key cities. Short-term order at a cost, the Reichsbanner will not be pleased.

The Reichsbanner are absolutely pissed.

@martial_law
on-arrival: month_actions +=1
view-if: military_concessions == 5
subtitle: If the devil want's to dance with you, you better say never.

Because the dance with the devil might last forever.

- @game_over: It is done.

@dvp_menu
view-if: dvp_alignment < 10 or dvp_in_government != 1

The DVP has declared it's neutrality, [? if violence_level < 33 : as of now it will stay that way as violence isn't widespread enough to concern them, but we can still build friendly relations with them. ?] [? if violence_level >= 33 : but with violence being widespread, they cannot stay neutral for long. ?]

[? if dvp_alignment == dvp_willing_alignment : We need to talk to them more about the specifics of them supporting us. Otherwise, they cannot be convinced of supporting us yet. ?]


- @talks: Engage in talks with the DVP, negotiating continued support.
- @left_wing: Strengthen the left wing of the DVP, making them more willing to support us.
- @root: Perhaps another time
- @easy_discard

@talks
on-arrival: dvp_willing_alignment += 2; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2

We continue on our talks with the DVP, they seem more willing to support us now.

@left_wing
subtitle: -1 resource [? if dvp_alignment == dvp_willing_alignment : Even if we did strengthen their leftwing, we need to negotiate more for them even consider supporting us. ?]
choose-if: dvp_alignment != dvp_willing_alignment and resources > 0
on-arrival: dvp_alignment += 1.5; month_actions +=1; paramilitaries_timer = 2; resources -= 1

Using contacts in the DVP's left wing, we have supported their faction through our own party resources.

